        {
          "widget": {
            "name": "method",
            "multilineTextboxSpec": {
              "lines": [
                "## How the share is calculated (method & caveats)**Duration-proportional allocation.** A SQL warehouse bills DBUs for *uptime*, not per query. For each warehouse-hour we split billed DBUs across every query by its share of active time: `genie_cost = hourly_DBUs × (genie_active_ms ÷ all_active_ms) × dbu_price`. Idle / keep-alive time is spread proportionally across active work.**Pricing:** DBUs are stored in the rollup; the `dbu_price` parameter converts to $ (NFCU net = $0.393/DBU ≈ 43.9% off the $0.70 list). **Why config matters:** `auto_stop` sets how long idle is billed after the last query; `min/max clusters` drive the Min→Max $/hr spread; a bigger size costs more per hour.*Estimate, not a bill. Reads a materialized hourly rollup (`main.mki_genie_cost.*`) refreshed from system tables. For exact numbers, run the space on a dedicated tagged serverless warehouse.*"
              ]
            }
          },
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 31,
            "width": 12,
            "height": 5
          }
        }
